  "title": "opcua: Fix heap-buffer-overflow in opcua_secrets_block_callback",
  "description": "## Summary\n\nFixes a heap-buffer-overflow (1-byte out-of-bounds read) in opcua_secrets_block_callback() in plugins/epan/opcua/opcua.c, found via local ASan/UBSan-instrumented fuzzing.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`char *tmp = g_memdup2(secrets, size + 1);`\n\ng_memdup2() both allocates **and copies** size + 1 bytes. The source buffer secrets only contains size valid bytes, so this reads 1 byte past the end of the source allocation. The extra byte was added purely as space for a manual null terminator.\n\n## Fix\n\nAllocate size + 1 zero-initialized bytes with g_malloc0(), but only copy the valid size bytes in with memcpy(). The zero-fill makes the null terminator implicit, so the manual tmp\\[size\\] = 0; line and the NULL OOM check are also removed (g_malloc0/g_malloc abort on allocation failure rather than returning NULL, per GLib semantics, so the guard was dead code).\n\n## How this was found\n\nBuilt locally with Clang + ASan + UBSan (-DENABLE_ASAN=1 -DENABLE_UBSAN=1), then ran tools/fuzz-test.sh against the existing sample captures in test/captures/. It reproducibly crashed on opcua-encrypted_with_chunking_with_keys.pcapng:\n\n==16457==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow on address 0x5130000022e4 READ of size 357 at 0x5130000022e4 thread T0 #0 memcpy #1 g_memdup2 #2 opcua_secrets_block_callback plugins/epan/opcua/opcua.c:877 #3 secrets_wtap_callback epan/secrets.c:189 #4 wtapng_process_dsb wiretap/wtap.c:1746 ... 0x5130000022e4 is located 0 bytes after 356-byte region \\[0x513000002180,0x5130000022e4) allocated by thread T0 here: #0 calloc #1 g_malloc0 #2 pcapng_read_block wiretap/pcapng.c:3314 ...\n\nConfirmed deterministic (356 bytes allocated, 357 read, every run). After the fix, the same capture dissects cleanly with no ASan errors.\n\n## Verification\n\n* Rebuilt (ninja) and re-ran tshark -nVxr against the crashing capture, clean output, no ASan abort\n* Re-ran tools/fuzz-test.sh against all test/captures/opcua\\*.pcap\\* samples, no regressions\n* Confirmed with ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0\n\nAI-Assisted: Yes (Claude), used to help set up the ASan/UBSan fuzzing environment.",
